2026-08-24 cold-review hardening

Review pass 1
- Split the rich WKWebView fixture into independent IR and SV processes to avoid Vditor mode-rebuild serialization hangs.
- Replaced DOM-dependent cross-renderer footnote reservations with a source parser that mirrors the Swift footnote preprocessor.
- Fixed CommonMark reference projection for first-definition-wins, escaped labels, Unicode case folding, and distinct NBSP labels.
- Added standalone export normalization for authored raw HTML IDs and headings.
- Made app-export scanning resume after self-closing SVG script/style/title elements.

Review pass 2
- Added a generated Unicode 17 full case-fold table; pinned sigma, eszett-compatible folding, and distinct Latin/dotless i.
- Modeled SVG and MathML integration points, conditional font breakout, foreign-content breakout, and raw-text behavior.
- Added WHATWG-style semicolonless named and numeric character-reference decoding, including C1 replacements.
- Made tag termination attribute-state-aware and heading closure tolerate mismatched heading end tags.
- Reserved authored raw HTML IDs before allocating generated footnote and back-reference IDs.
- Added the Unicode License V3 notice.

Review pass 3
- Scoped integration-point names to their actual SVG or MathML namespace.
- Decoded entity-bearing annotation-xml encoding values.
- Reprocessed foreign heading end tags against the underlying HTML heading.
- Tracked HTML descendants of foreign integration points so mglyph/malignmark exceptions apply only to an immediate MathML parent.
- Made semantic heading text namespace-aware for SVG title descendants.
- Reserved IDs from de-indented footnote definition bodies before footnote allocation.

Convergence
- Final cold review reported no significant issues in the amended surfaces.
- Focused Swift regression tests passed.
- Independent IR and SV WKWebView contracts passed.
